The nine test_wycheproof*.sh drivers in this directory share nothing: each
is `ae run <vectors>.ae` with no output paths, no ports and no build
artifacts, so `make test-ae` schedules each as a unit of its own instead of
running them one after another on one worker (#2132 §5). The longest,
ecdsa_p521, then bounds the shell phase instead of the sum of all nine.

A directory WITHOUT this file runs its drivers serially: two drivers in one
directory may share fixed ports (http_reverse_proxy_pool: 19101-19103) or
build outputs, and the per-directory unit is what keeps them apart.
